---
/**
 * The answer to the question readers bring: can one satellite image see what is claimed under Khafre? Built from the
 * claim computed for its own geometry (P2-38), the published method read blind on images of known ground (P2-37) and the
 * proof's bounds; every number is the runs' own. A statement, three numbers, what it rests on, what could change it.
 */
import claim from '../../public/data/runs/p2_38_claim.json';
import read from '../../public/data/runs/p2_37_benchmark_read.json';

interface Props { heading?: 'h2' | 'h3' }
const { heading = 'h2' } = Astro.props;
const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL.replace(/\/$/, '');

type ClRow = { l1: Record<string, { tv_upper: number }>; oracle_power_weighted: Record<string, { tv_upper: number }>; l1_growth_to_target: number | null; oracle_growth_to_target: number };
type ClPass = { headline_db: number; parts: Record<string, { rows: Record<string, ClRow> }> };
const cl25 = (claim as unknown as { passes: Record<string, ClPass> }).passes['giza-20250827'];
const key = String(cl25.headline_db);
const row = cl25.parts['claim (both)'].rows['as computed'];
const l1 = row.l1[key].tv_upper;
const orGrowth = row.oracle_growth_to_target;
type RdR = { named_of_three: number };
const rd = (read as unknown as { summary: Record<string, { told: RdR; published_blind: RdR }>; manifest: { params: { grounds: number[] } } });
const pos = rd.summary['x1000'];
const nGrounds = rd.manifest.params.grounds.length;

const inWords = (n: number) =>
  n >= 1e9 ? `${+(n / 1e9).toPrecision(2)} billion` : n >= 1e6 ? `${+(n / 1e6).toPrecision(2)} million` : n >= 1e3 ? `${+(n / 1e3).toPrecision(2)} thousand` : `${Math.round(n)}`;
const times = (v: number) => Number(v.toPrecision(2)).toLocaleString('en-US');
const pc = (v: number) => `${Math.round(100 * v)}%`;
const H = heading;
---
<div class="claim-verdict">
  <p class="cv-label">The question readers bring</p>
  <H class="cv-title">Can one satellite radar image see the shafts and chambers claimed under Khafre? In our assessment, no</H>
  <p class="cv-lede">
    Not with the published method, and not with any other way of reading one image. We computed the claimed structures
    themselves, at their claimed depths, and the trace they leave in the image is far below anything a reading could pick out.
  </p>
  <div class="stat-row">
    <div class="stat"><span class="value">1 in {inWords(1 / l1)}</span><span class="what">the most any way of reading one image of Khafre can do better than a coin toss at telling whether the claimed shafts and void are there: the published method, any future algorithm, a trained network</span><span class="src">P2-38 · computed for the claim · an upper bound</span></div>
    <div class="stat"><span class="value">{times(orGrowth)}<small>×</small></span><span class="what">how much more the claimed structures would have to move the ground before even a reader told every detail of the scene except the answer could find them reliably</span><span class="src">P2-38 · the oracle · most favourable noise floor</span></div>
    <div class="stat"><span class="value">{pc(pos.published_blind.named_of_three)}</span><span class="what">how often the published method names the right buried layout on images of known ground, the cavity’s effect amplified a thousandfold: chance. A detector told what to look for names {pc(pos.told.named_of_three)}</span><span class="src">P2-37 · blind · {nGrounds} grounds</span></div>
  </div>
  <div class="cv-cols">
    <div>
      <p class="cv-sub">What the assessment rests on</p>
      <p>Calculations on a model of the ground, not field measurements: uniform limestone, the trembling measured 67 km
      away, the radar maker’s most favourable noise figure, the claim’s own depths and a representative layout, with the
      pyramid left out, which helps the claim. The bound covers every way of reading one image, not only the published one;
      the 2022 paper was retracted in August 2026.</p>
    </div>
    <div>
      <p class="cv-sub">What could still change it</p>
      <p>A mechanism nobody has yet specified that makes the ground move thousands of times more over a void; a bright fixture
      over a cavity beside strong shaking, the one case these bounds leave open; or a method shown to find surveyed voids
      blind, on ground withheld from it. None has been shown.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
  <p class="cv-links"><a href={`${base}/proof/`}>The proof, finite and stated →</a> · <a href={`${base}/satellite/`}>every test, on the satellite page →</a></p>
</div>

<style>
  .claim-verdict {
    max-width: var(--page, 1040px);
    margin: 0 auto;
  }
  .cv-label {
    font: 600 10.5px/1.4 var(--font-mono);
    letter-spacing: 0.7px;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--muted);
    margin: 0 0 6px;
  }
  .cv-title {
    font-family: var(--font-serif);
    font-size: clamp(22px, 3vw, 30px);
    font-weight: 500;
    line-height: 1.2;
    color: var(--text);
    margin: 0 0 10px;
    max-width: 30ch;
  }
  h3.cv-title {
    font-size: clamp(20px, 2.4vw, 24px);
    max-width: 40ch;
  }
  .cv-lede {
    font-family: var(--font-serif);
    font-size: 16px;
    line-height: 1.55;
    color: var(--body);
    margin: 0 0 16px;
    max-width: 70ch;
  }
  .cv-cols {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;
    gap: 22px;
    margin-top: 16px;
  }
  .cv-cols p {
    font-family: var(--font-serif);
    font-size: 14.5px;
    line-height: 1.55;
    color: var(--body);
    margin: 0;
  }
  .cv-cols .cv-sub {
    font: 600 10.5px/1.4 var(--font-mono);
    letter-spacing: 0.6px;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--muted);
    margin: 0 0 4px;
  }
  .cv-links {
    font: 12px var(--font-mono);
    margin: 14px 0 0;
  }
  @media (max-width: 760px) {
    .cv-cols {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }
  }
  @media (max-width: 600px) {
    .stat-row {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }
  }
</style>
